# Copy to .env.local for local development. `.env*.local` is gitignored; this
# file is the record of what the console reads.

# ── API target ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Same-origin default: leave BOTH unset and the UI talks to its own origin,
# and (in the single-URL demo) the backend answers from behind the same host.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE — direct backend origin for local dev (bypasses any
# proxy, e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8000). When this is unset/empty the UI uses
# relative paths and `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_PROXY_TARGET` (server-only) is used by
# the Next rewrite to forward to the backend.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_PROXY_TARGET — optional; server-side rewrite target. Only
# needed when the UI and backend are on different origins in production and
# you want Next to proxy rather than expose the backend directly.

# Local dev, no proxy:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# Production (single-URL demo): both unset; backend and UI share an origin.
